# Rules live in `/CLAUDE.md`

This repo keeps **one** rule set, at [`/CLAUDE.md`](../../CLAUDE.md). Read it before acting.

There is deliberately no second copy here. The previous round drifted apart across 24 rule
files totalling 82 KB, most of them always-on, and that is what made the project re-decide the
same questions over and over.

Short version:

- Source of truth: [`docs/NewConcept/`](../../docs/NewConcept/README.md). `docs/legacy/` is frozen.
- **No production code** until `docs/NewConcept/10-domain-core.md` has status `locked`.
- Nothing is decided until it is in `docs/NewConcept/90-decision-log.md`.
- Unclear goes to `docs/NewConcept/91-open-questions.md`. Never invent an answer.
- An architecture rule requires a decision id. No `D-<nnn>`, no rule.

Do not add rule files here. Add rules to `/CLAUDE.md`, under its hygiene section.
